# Privacy Policy — Shopping List

_Last updated: November 22, 2026_

Shopping List organizes your shopping lists, keeps the prices you pay at each store and shows what
the trip will cost. It was made to work with no account, no server and no internet: **what you
enter stays on your phone**. This policy explains what the app uses, why, and what happens on the
free plan, which shows ads.

## 1. What stays on your phone

Lists, items, categories, prices, stores, past trips, templates, reminders and your settings are
stored only on the device. Reminders are scheduled on the phone itself. We have no server, create no
account and never receive a copy of this data. The app keeps this data out of the system's automatic
backups (Android and iCloud).

## 2. Permissions

Each permission is requested only when you use the feature, and the app keeps working if you say
no. Shopping List never asks for location, the camera, photos, contacts or the calendar.

| Permission | What for |
|---|---|
| Notifications | Remind you of your lists and trips at the time you choose. |
| Exact alarm (Android) | Make the reminder arrive at the set time, also after a restart. |
| Files | Save and open the backup and the spreadsheet, always through the system file picker. |

## 3. Backups, spreadsheet and sharing

Backups, the spreadsheet (CSV) and the lists you share are files or messages that **you** create and
send wherever you like (email, cloud, messages). The Premium automatic copy, on the 1st of every
month, is kept in a folder on the phone itself. Once you send something, the policy of the service
you chose applies.

An email to support only carries what you write and, if you leave the option on, the phone model and
versions; the email is sent from your own email app.

## 4. Ads (free plan)

The free plan shows ads from **Google AdMob**. To show and measure ads and to prevent fraud, Google
may collect the device's advertising ID, the IP address (and the approximate location derived from
it), technical device and system details, interactions with ads (such as app launches, taps and
video views) and diagnostic data about the app and the SDK.

- Where the law requires it (such as the European Economic Area, the UK and Switzerland), the app
  asks for your consent first through Google's consent platform, and you can change your choice
  later.
- On iPhone, the system asks whether the app may track you across apps; without permission, the
  advertising ID is not used and ads continue without personalization.
- None of your lists or prices go to the ad network.
- With **Premium** there are no ads and the ads SDK is not started.

How Google uses this data: <https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites>.

## 5. Purchases

Subscriptions and the lifetime purchase are processed by **Google Play** or the **App Store**. We
never receive your payment details; the app only asks the store whether Premium is active. The
prices you type for your shopping are only notes on the phone.

## 6. Internet

The app uses the internet only for ads (free plan) and the store (purchases and restore
purchases). Everything else works offline.

## 7. Children

The app is not directed to children under 13 and does not knowingly collect children's data.

## 8. Retention and deletion

Data stays on the phone until you delete it. What you delete goes to the trash and stays there for
30 days before it is deleted for good. **Settings › Backup & data › Erase all data** makes the app
like new; uninstalling the app also deletes everything. Backups and spreadsheets you exported stay
wherever you saved them. Since we keep none of your data, there is nothing to delete on our side;
requests about ad data can be made to Google in the ad settings of your account or device.

## 9. Your rights

You have the rights provided by the LGPD (Brazil), the GDPR (Europe) and similar laws. Write to us at
the email below with any question or request; we reply within 30 days.

## 10. Changes

If this policy changes, the date at the top is updated and relevant changes are announced in the app.

